WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.160
- You know, President Obama,
once when I had him on the

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:03.990
you know I called him
the week he announced

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:05.130
before anybody knew who he was

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:08.130
to invite him on the
Tonight Show, you know, and

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:09.840
'cause everybody thought
Hillary had it in the bag,

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.557
you know, so he came in and he go,

00:00:11.557 --> 00:00:13.140
"Jay, my name's Barack Hussein Obama

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:15.330
I'm running for president
of the United States."

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.490
I said, "Okay, well let's
look at the odds here.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.829
Black guy named Hussein from Chicago.

00:00:19.829 --> 00:00:20.662
(audience laughs)

00:00:20.662 --> 00:00:21.495
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:21.495 --> 00:00:22.328
Nobody ever heard of him.

00:00:22.328 --> 00:00:23.550
Ah, you're gonna win pal.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:24.660
You're gonna be a shoe in."

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.580
You know, and you know, he was very funny.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:27.856
He had a great time.

00:00:27.856 --> 00:00:28.905
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:28.905 --> 00:00:30.450
So he and I became friends and he gave

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:32.040
he gave me his cell phone number.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.470
So I said, one day I'm telling my friend,

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:35.303
now you know how this is

00:00:35.303 --> 00:00:36.600
when you come from a small town

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.150
you have the same idiot
friends your whole life

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:40.260
that you grew up with, you know.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:41.167
So I'm telling my friends, you know,

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:42.307
"I got Obama's cell phone."

00:00:42.307 --> 00:00:43.200
"Let's call him up."

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.420
You know, I go "We're not gonna call him."

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:46.905
He goes, "You don't have it, nuh-uh."

00:00:46.905 --> 00:00:47.738
"Uh huh."

00:00:47.738 --> 00:00:48.571
"Nuh uh."

00:00:48.571 --> 00:00:49.404
"Uh huh."

00:00:49.404 --> 00:00:50.700
I'm a, like, 45 year old
man, and we're going,

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.350
"Nuh uh, uh huh, nuh uh."

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:54.660
Okay. So finally my friend
said, "No, you don't have it."

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:55.650
I said, "First of all

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:58.117
it's probably shut off
since he's President."

00:00:58.117 --> 00:01:00.270
"Well if he shut it off, let's call it."

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:02.108
I said, "What time, it's
three o'clock in California.

00:01:02.108 --> 00:01:03.840
Okay, so it's 12. All right."

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.280
I dial the number.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.297
I hear, "Barack here."

00:01:07.297 --> 00:01:10.477
"Oh, Mr. President? Yeah, it's Jay Leno."

00:01:10.477 --> 00:01:12.307
"What can I do for you, Jay?"

00:01:12.307 --> 00:01:13.417
"Should I throw this number away?"

00:01:13.417 --> 00:01:14.692
"Good idea, Jay."

00:01:14.692 --> 00:01:17.640
(audience laughs and claps)

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.070
- I was like, you didn't have a plan?

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:20.903
- No I had,

00:01:20.903 --> 00:01:22.140
I didn't think he was
gonna answer the phone!

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:23.167
- Oh my God, you have,

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:25.317
"Oh, well I was just calling
about the crisis and,

00:01:25.317 --> 00:01:26.520
and if you needed any help,"

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:27.660
like, you know. (laughs)

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:28.560
- Exactly.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:29.520
- Oh my God. (laughs)

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:30.870
None of my friends care what I do.

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:32.130
They don't care whose
number I have. (laughs)

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.740
I'm not cool. Your friends
still think you're cool.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.030
- Well, no, they don't
really think I'm cool.

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:37.549
But, but you know what it is

00:01:37.549 --> 00:01:38.382
- It's pretty cool to have Barack

00:01:38.382 --> 00:01:40.380
- When you have the same
idiot friends that you

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:41.640
- 100%.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:42.473
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:42.473 --> 00:01:43.306
- I mean, I'm not calling them idiots.

00:01:43.306 --> 00:01:46.064
So shout out April, Mary. (laughs)

00:01:46.064 --> 00:01:47.790
- I'm, I'm calling mine idiots.

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:48.870
